<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundle's own Info.plist by tauri-bundler on macOS.

  This file exists for one key, and the key is not optional: macOS terminates a
  process that opens an input stream without a usage description for it. Not a
  refusal that can be caught and reported — the app is killed — so choosing an
  input device without this is the app disappearing mid-performance.

  The string is what the permission dialog says, and it is the only thing a
  person has to go on when deciding. So it says what the microphone is for
  rather than that one is wanted.

  Nothing here covers `tauri dev`, which runs a bare binary with no bundle: on
  a development machine the permission is the terminal's, granted once and
  attributed there.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Swync uses the audio input you choose in its settings panel so that a live signal — a microphone, an instrument, an interface — can be played and processed by your programs.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
